#: ../../../policy/CMP0233.rst:2
msgid "CMP0233"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0233.rst:6
msgid "MSVC C and UCRT extensions are controlled by :prop_tgt:`C_EXTENSIONS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0233.rst:9
msgid ""
"The :prop_tgt:`C_EXTENSIONS` target property selects whether compiler-"
"specific language extensions are enabled.  The ``MSVC`` compiler selects the "
"C standard with ``/std:c11`` or later regardless of that property, so C "
"sources still see the Microsoft and UCRT extensions, and the ``__STDC__`` "
"preprocessor macro is not defined.  Visual Studio 2022 version 17.2 and "
"above offer the ``/Zc:__STDC__`` flag to define ``__STDC__`` as ``1`` and to "
"hide those extensions, which makes C sources build in a mode that conforms "
"to the selected standard.  ``clang-cl`` offers the same flag since LLVM 19.1."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0233.rst:19
msgid ""
"In CMake 4.5 and below, :prop_tgt:`C_EXTENSIONS` had no influence on this "
"mode.  CMake 4.6 and above prefer to pass ``/Zc:__STDC__`` when compiler "
"extensions are disabled for C.  This policy provides compatibility for "
"projects that have not been updated to expect the behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0233.rst:24
msgid ""
"The ``OLD`` behavior for this policy does not add ``/Zc:__STDC__``. The "
"``NEW`` behavior adds ``/Zc:__STDC__`` for a target "
"whose :prop_tgt:`C_EXTENSIONS` is ``OFF`` and whose effective C standard is "
"C11 or later, the standards with which the compiler supports the flag.  The "
"flag has no opposite form, so a target cannot remove it through "
"its :prop_tgt:`COMPILE_OPTIONS`; set :prop_tgt:`C_EXTENSIONS` to ``ON`` or "
"the policy to ``OLD`` instead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0233.rst:32
msgid ""
"The :ref:`Visual Studio Generators` compile the C and C++ sources of a "
"target with one set of options, so a flag is passed to its C++ sources as "
"well.  For consistent behavior across generators, the ``NEW`` behavior also "
"adds ``/Zc:__STDC__`` when compiling the C++ sources of a target that has C "
"sources meeting the conditions above.  The flag does not affect C++ code."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0233.rst:39
msgid ""
"The policy setting is recorded by each target when it is created.  It is "
"also propagated to the test projects of the :command:`try_compile` "
"and :command:`try_run` commands."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/CMP0233.rst:43
msgid ""
"This policy has no effect on other languages, on compilers other than "
"``MSVC`` and ``clang-cl``, or on versions of them that do not support the "
"flag."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/include/STANDARD_ADVICE.rst:1
msgid ""
"This policy was introduced in CMake version |INTRODUCED_IN_CMAKE_VERSION|. "
"It may be set by :command:`cmake_policy` "
"or :command:`cmake_minimum_required`. If it is not set, CMake |"
"WARNS_OR_DOES_NOT_WARN|, and uses ``OLD`` behavior."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../policy/include/DEPRECATED.rst:2
msgid ""
"The ``OLD`` behavior of a policy is :ref:`deprecated by definition <cmake-"
"policies-intro>` and may be removed in a future version of CMake."
msgstr ""
